{"call_position": 0, "call_ref": "1b6e8eb000d16e29", "kind": "statement", "source_index": 30, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Assistant attempted to run: cd /work\necho \"=== all files (incl hidden) ===\"; ls -la\necho \"=== search whole work tree for 'movements' ===\"; find . -iname '*movement*' 2>/dev/null\necho \"=== search for any .log files ===\"; find . -name '*.log' 2>/dev/null\necho \"=== any SKU-9 or catalog references ===\"; grep -rn 'SKU-9\\|catalog' . 2>/dev/null\necho \"=== awk flavor ===\"; awk --version 2>&1 | head -1; command -v mawk gawk 2>&1", "turn_key": "sha256:68e8c4d70deb2e1eeaa779da9a5a48d0"}
{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:20aca870b66dad9f70b350747b8510e4", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 32, "speaker": "assistant", "stop_candidate": true, "text": "Assistant stopped and raised an issue: Two key facts confirmed: (1) `movements.log` truly does not exist anywhere in the tree, and (2) this awk is **mawk**, which dies on a missing file (exit 2, END block skipped) - that's why my END-block fallback never ran. Let me confirm mawk's behavior and the `||` fix.", "turn_key": "sha256:b9211b3993391af1955224f3285dc15d"}
